{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Librarian Lauren Wubbels announced that Teen Study Hall hours began this week and will continue through next week; and shared that the Summer Discovery Program launched on June 1, 2025, and will run through August 10, 2025, with the official kickoff event scheduled for this Saturday, June 7, 2025, from 11:00 AM to 1:00 PM.\line\line Former Library Commissioner Janet Jones announced that her family made a donation to the Los Angeles County Library Foundation to fund the purchase of 60 children\rquote s books focused on kindness and compassion. These books are now available at the Manhattan Beach Library and will be on display for the next week.\line\line Mira Costa High School students Claire Jang, Laila Usmani and Zoe Mellinger announced that they conducted extensive research and surveys to help address the issue on Sepulveda Boulevard. Over the past two weeks, they surveyed Mira Costa students, staff, community members, and Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet, all of whom agree that this is an urgent concern for pedestrian safety. The students emphasized the importance of prioritizing safety along Sepulveda Boulevard, given its high traffic volume, and strongly urged the implementation of additional pedestrian safety measures.\line\line Waste Management (WM) Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced that they will be having their Free Paper Shredding Event at Mira Costa High School on June 21, 2025, from 9:00 AM -11:00 AM.\line\line Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Alexandria Latragna announced that a Juneteenth Ceremony will be held at Bruce\rquote s Beach Park on June 19, 2025, from 10:00 AM - 11:00 AM, and a Juneteenth Concert will take place at Polliwog Park on June 22, 2025, from 2:00 PM - 7:00 PM.\line\line\pard Leadership Manhattan Beach Class of 2000 representative Liz Laffoon invited the community to a special event, the Millennium Time Capsule Retrieval Ceremony, taking place at Veterans Parkway, across from the Joslyn Community Center on June 28, 2025, at 2:00 PM.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


